WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:06.060
He caught their voices, but now Brian the Boom&nbsp;
Mic Guy is breaking his silence. Or, at least,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:11.592
actor Chris Diamontopoulos has some words to say&nbsp;
about his controversial character on "The Office."

00:00:11.592 --> 00:00:16.140
Who would have thought that a simple boom mic&nbsp;
guy trying to make a PBS documentary would cause&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:21.960
so much tension within the "Office" fandom? Okay,&nbsp;
so Chris isn't actually a boom mic operator — but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:27.020
his character did cause a significant hurdle for&nbsp;
one of TV's most beloved mockumentary couples.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:31.380
But really, can you blame a guy for developing&nbsp;
heart eyes for Pam Beesley? After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.640
Jim Halpert can certainly relate. But&nbsp;
after years of waiting for Pam and Jim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:39.778
to get together, fans wanted no part&nbsp;
of any threats to their relationship.

00:00:39.778 --> 00:00:44.520
When the couple finally defines the relationship&nbsp;
in Season 4, it's smooth sailing from Niagara&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:50.220
Falls and beyond. But then, enter Brian, the Boom&nbsp;
Mic Guy, who steps out in front of the cameras to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:55.287
shake things up in Season 9 when Pam and Jim&nbsp;
are constantly fighting about Jim's new job.

00:00:55.287 --> 00:01:00.000
Looper exclusively spoke to Diamantopoulos,&nbsp;
who set the record straight about Brian and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.780
the fans who love to hate him. At&nbsp;
the mention of his hotly contested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.740
role on "The Office," Chris jokingly&nbsp;
apologized. The actor also agreed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:11.572
seeing the couple go through their first&nbsp;
realistic hurdle since coupling was nice.

00:01:11.572 --> 00:01:16.140
On what he would say to "The Office" fans who&nbsp;
threw shade at Brian for getting between Jim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.120
and Pam with such a meta storyline, Chris wants&nbsp;
fans to realize that not everything is perfect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.908
even in the healthiest relationships. He said,

00:01:23.908 --> 00:01:28.200
"First of all, I would say, 'Wake up and smell&nbsp;
the reality, folks.' ... In every relationship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:33.489
you got to put the extra work in. Sometimes things&nbsp;
go by the wayside, and yeah, that's reality."

00:01:33.489 --> 00:01:37.500
"Let's turn the cameras off.&nbsp;
Seriously, guys. Enough. Enough."

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:43.440
And for anyone who tends to forget, actors&nbsp;
are not their characters. It's super uncool&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:47.340
to harass an actor just because you don't&nbsp;
like their character. Chris continued,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:52.380
"The other thing I would say to them is, 'Hey,&nbsp;
people watching screens — I'm an actor. I didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:57.240
try to break up Jim and Pam. I didn't do this.&nbsp;
I was hired.' The last thing I would say is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.920
'You can see in Pam's eyes that she's a little&nbsp;
more into Brian. I'm sorry. She doesn't go there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.660
but she wanted to. So you know&nbsp;
what, guys? Sorry, but f--k you.'"

00:02:05.808 --> 00:02:07.260
Of course, if you've ever met Chris,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:12.115
you'd know that he has a sardonic sense of&nbsp;
humor. So don't go picketing his house, okay?

00:02:12.115 --> 00:02:15.780
Chris also wants to assure fans&nbsp;
that Brian's doing great. He joked,

00:02:16.128 --> 00:02:20.268
"Brian's living in the Turks and Caicos.&nbsp;
He's a fly fisherman. He's really good."

00:02:20.268 --> 00:02:22.200
Though fans can be savage about Brian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.040
Chris loved working with John Krasinski&nbsp;
and Jenna Fischer. He told Looper,

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:30.720
"They are pros to the nth degree, and I'm such&nbsp;
a fan of what John and Jenna did both on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.920
show and how their careers have exploded —&nbsp;
rightfully so — off the show. I showed up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:39.720
on that set very penitent and deferential with&nbsp;
the notion that I am here to help if I could."

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:44.640
Chris foresaw that there would be fan resistance&nbsp;
when he signed on, but that's the gig.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.020
"I knew that any instance where the character&nbsp;
pushed into the territory where the audience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:53.340
might perceive that there's a threat there would&nbsp;
leave me, the actor, probably being reviled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:57.600
but that's my job ... As a fan of the show, it&nbsp;
broke my heart to see their marriage in trouble,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:01.425
but as a professional actor, I was&nbsp;
ready to give Jim a run for his money."

